Z||000011||sparks||02-22-2001||11:45 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by WampusCat:<BR><B>Somebody should tell those Yahoos that the DeLorean was manufacuted in Ireland and the Pantera was manufactured in Italy.  Yeah, they were sold in Ford dealerships but that didn't make them American-built cars.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>done. <P>Don't know that they'll listen tho.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Sheesh, I didn't know that we Jeep owners were so ignorant or close minded.  Been a Jeep owner a lot longer than a Fiero owner and didn't think twice about buying a Fiero to drive on my occasional long commute in place of my Wrangler.<P><P>------------------<BR><BR>Adam Sparks||||reg||1
Z||000012||Jaygee79||02-22-2001||04:44 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Black88GT:<BR><B>The one MR2 owner mentions a Car and Driver article that never existed.  Car and Driver only tested the Formula vs. CRX vs. MR2 N/A in June 88 I believe.  The other mag tested MR2 S/C vs. a Formula, forget which one, I think it was Road and Track.  So no GT was ever tested in 88 against an MR2, I dont feel like registering just to set that guy straight.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I don't know about magazines, but Motorweek tested the 88 Fiero and the 88 MR2 against eachother.  The Fiero Store sells the video.  They were rather comparable, but the Fiero was the overall winner.||||reg||1
